From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:19:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/32] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: record 24-bit samples on the
 OnePlus Pad 4

The microphones of the OnePlus Pad 4 reach the DSP through
TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3, which the back-end fixup runs at 16 bit. Stock
records them with 24-bit samples. Run the TX codec DMA back end with
S24_LE (24 bits in a 32-bit word) on this board, so a 32-bit front end
gets the converters' low-order bits instead of 16-bit quantisation
noise, which the post-processing gain otherwise lifts.

Only the OnePlus Pad 4 card sets the flag; other Kaanapali boards are
unchanged until it is checked on them.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index a4f2a8a973b6..f8cd37d61c47 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -95,6 +95,7 @@ struct qcom_snd_soc_common {
 	bool mi2s_bclk_enable;
 	bool wcd_jack;
 	bool rx_codec_dma_s24;
+	bool tx_codec_dma_s24;
 	const struct sc8280xp_dai_data *dai_data;
 	size_t num_dai_data;
 	int (*snd_init)(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd);
@@ -311,6 +312,11 @@ static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_2:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3:
 		channels->min = 1;
+		/* 24-bit ADC samples in 32-bit words, as stock records them */
+		if (data->priv->tx_codec_dma_s24) {
+			snd_mask_none(fmt);
+			snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S24_LE);
+		}
 		break;
 	case RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0:
 		/*
@@ -631,6 +637,7 @@ static struct qcom_snd_soc_common oneplus_iceland_priv_data = {
 	.snd_prepare = oneplus_iceland_snd_prepare,
 	.wcd_jack = true,
 	.rx_codec_dma_s24 = true,
+	.tx_codec_dma_s24 = true,
 };
 
 static const struct qcom_snd_soc_common eliza_priv_data = {
